// REJECTS: Field 'persistence' is required
//
// A PersistenceContext has exactly one required field -- `persistence:`, the element it is a
// context FOR -- and the `context` rule is the usual unordered star over all four, so a
// context that configures a sink connection and names nothing to apply it to parses.
###Persistence
PersistenceContext test::persistence::neg::ContextNoPersistence
{
  sinkConnection: test::persistence::TestConnection;
}
